:: BetterThings {"title":"Ending 1 / Toward Better Things","scene":"dawn"}
@do $ending = "Toward Better Things"

# Toward Better Things

@Chapter("ENDING 1 OF 6", "Distance, with witnesses")

Mars takes the company job. You stop checking whether the spare key has moved.

Three months later you meet at a diner halfway between her apartment and your house.
She pays for coffee. You pay for pie. Neither expense becomes evidence.

When she kisses you in the parking lot, both of you have somewhere else to sleep.
It is not a happy ending. It is the first ending that does not need either woman to lose.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="clear"}
**TOWARD BETTER THINGS**

Unlocked by trust, honesty, and the terrifying possibility of separate lives.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: KeyReturned {"title":"Ending 2 / A Key Returned","scene":"dawn"}
@do $ending = "A Key Returned"

# A Key Returned

@Chapter("ENDING 2 OF 6", "No debt collected")

Mars leaves the spare key on the table. You slide it back.

“For emergencies,” you say.

“Whose?”

You do not answer. She takes the key anyway, but not the room. On Tuesday she drives
a white truck with matching doors. You learn not to call every silence abandonment.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="quiet"}
**A KEY RETURNED**

Care is not clean just because nobody sends an invoice.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: TermsAndConditions {"title":"Ending 3 / Terms and Conditions","scene":"yard"}
@do $ending = "Terms and Conditions"

# Terms and Conditions

@Chapter("ENDING 3 OF 6", "Read before signing")

The new company is boring on purpose. Roadside starts. Tire changes. Legal recovery.
Each woman owns half; either can leave with thirty days' notice.

Mars adds one handwritten clause: **NO THERAPY LANGUAGE DURING PAYROLL**.

You add another: **NO BOYFRIENDS WITH BOLT CUTTERS**.

The signatures are cautious. So is the first kiss after.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="clear"}
**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**

The paperwork is clean. The people remain complicated.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: BusinessPartners {"title":"Ending 4 / Unfortunately","scene":"yard"}
@do $ending = "Unfortunately"

# Unfortunately

@Chapter("ENDING 4 OF 6", "Co-applicants")

The lender asks your relationship.

You write **BUSINESS PARTNERS**. Mars adds **UNFORTUNATELY**. The clerk points to the
box for married applicants and says everybody tells him that after the credit check.

You buy a funeral-home tow truck with gold wings beneath the black paint. The loan
can take the vehicle, your equipment, and half the house.

This is not a wedding. For both of you, it is close enough.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="amber"}
**UNFORTUNATELY**

Love survives as a jointly held liability.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: WomenOwned {"title":"Ending 5 / Women-Owned","scene":"yard"}
@do $ending = "Women-Owned"

# Women-Owned

@Chapter("ENDING 5 OF 6", "The numbers work")

Sister Shift expands. The card reader asks impounded drivers to add a 20, 25, or 30
percent tip. The **NO TIP** button asks if they are sure.

One winter morning, a nurse begs you not to take the car she needs for work. Her
parking pass expired yesterday. A sick child watches from an upstairs window.

Mars lowers the hook.

“Are we bad people?” she asks once the building disappears behind you.

“We are a women-owned business,” you say.

Both of you laugh because stopping would require an answer.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="red"}
**WOMEN-OWNED**

The truck is finally legal. Nothing else is.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: HonestWreck {"title":"Ending 6 / The Honest Wreck","scene":"dawn"}
@do $ending = "The Honest Wreck"

# The Honest Wreck

@Chapter("ENDING 6 OF 6", "Nothing to tow")

Mars takes the key but not the room. The house is silent for weeks.

On Wednesdays you keep arranging chairs. Eventually two people arrive. You tell
them the group has no answers tonight. Nobody leaves.

Mars does not come back. She sends a photograph of a white recovery truck from an
unknown number. You do not save it under evidence.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="quiet"}
**THE HONEST WRECK**

Some endings are only clean because they leave nothing attached.
:::

[[Review the case file -> CaseNotes]]

[[Begin again -> Start]]

:: LockedRoom {"title":"Ending 0 / The Locked Room","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $ending = "The Locked Room"

# The Locked Room

@Chapter("BAD END", "The safest place")

Mars leaves. Three weeks later she returns with a split lip and no truck. You hand
her frozen peas and do not ask whose fault it was, because both possible answers
frighten you.

She sleeps beside you with the width of another person between your bodies.

In the morning you discuss a loan.

::: ending {.ending-card tone="red"}
**THE LOCKED ROOM**

She returned. You decide not to ask whether that means you won.
:::

